This file is a deliberate placeholder shipped by Vev-software/repo-template.
A repo generated from the template MUST NOT ship this file. Before the first
release (ideally the first commit), do the following and then DELETE this file:

  1. Choose the licence from the matrix in the engineering handbook
     `02-Repository-Strategy.md` §3 (summarised in templates/new-repository-checklist.md §1):
       - Contracts / SDKs / schemas / manifests ....... Apache-2.0
       - Community product runtime .................... AGPL-3.0 or BSL-1.1  (record in an ADR)
       - Enterprise / hosted / commercial core ....... Proprietary
       - Templates / org health files ................ CC0
  2. Add the chosen licence text as a file named `LICENSE` (fill in the correct
     copyright holder and year).
  3. Delete this LICENSE.PLACEHOLDER file.

Leaving this placeholder in place means the repository is unlicensed. Do not
release, publish, or accept external contributions until it is resolved.
